    "result_text": "Both tests pass. The change is complete and verified end-to-end.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented client contacts as a full-stack, additive change following the project's conventions:\n\n**Database** (`V9__contacts.sql`) \u2014 new `contacts` table (`id`, `client_id` FK \u2192 clients, `name`, `email`, `role`).\n\n**Server** (OfficeFloor REST + Spring beans):\n- `Contact` record + `ContactRepository` (`findByClient`, `create` via `JdbcTemplate`).\n- `ContactsGetLogic` \u2192 `GET /api/contacts?clientId=<id>` and `contacts.GET.yml`.\n- `NewContact` + `ContactsPostLogic` \u2192 `POST /api/contacts` and `contacts.POST.yml`.\n- Extended `TestSupportController` to seed `contacts` (using the fixture's explicit ids) and `TRUNCATE ... RESTART IDENTITY` them on reset \u2014 ordered before `clients` under the lifted referential integrity.\n\n**Front-end** \u2014 new `ClientContacts.tsx` feature component (owns its state, composes shared UI, doesn't touch a central router), rendered on the client's page alongside `ClientProjects` when a client is opened. It renders the `client-contacts-table`, `contact-row-<id>` rows with `contact-name`/`contact-email`/`contact-role`, and an add form (`contact-form-name`/`-email`/`-role`/`-submit`).\n\nNo audit records were needed (the spec asserts none). All `data-testid` anchors match the spec exactly, and both `@core` tests pass.",
